      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T23:16:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are 3 types:\n1. Signed for which we have a key (GKI modules built at the build time with build time key)\n2. Signed by any other key.\n3. Unsigned\n\nSIG_FORCE rejects #2 and #3. This option modifies that behavior of SIG_FORCE whose help says, \"Reject unsigned modules or signed modules for which we don\u0027t have a key.\" (Line#2200 above)\n\nThis option doesn\u0027t reject but allows it as long as symbol protection is not violated. If violated then loading will fail.\n\nHow about this?\n\n\"Modifies the behavior of CONFIG_SIG_FORCE by allowing loading of unsigned modules or signed modules for which we don\u0027t have a key if they don\u0027t violate the access to Android GKI protected symbols and do not export the symbols already exported by the Android GKI modules.\"",
      "parentUuid": "2a629a27_99d16faf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2210,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 2211,
